WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.958
Diabetes

00:00:00.958 --> 00:00:01.541
Coronary disease.

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:02.333
Autoimmune disease. 

00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:02.791
Obesity.

00:00:02.791 --> 00:00:03.500
Cancer.

00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:07.208
Pretty much all chronic 
diseases of the western world

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:11.375
are associated with a gut microbiome
that is unhealthy.

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:14.625
The good news is we 
can actually heal our gut. 

00:00:22.166 --> 00:00:25.833
This class is an exploration 
of the universe inside you

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:27.750
and how your gut 
impacts your mind,

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.041
your body and your life.

00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:32.041
The microbiome is so 
integrated in all aspects of health, 

00:00:32.041 --> 00:00:35.125
including mental health.

00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:38.083
We've realized that 
things like moods and behaviors 

00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:40.750
can be dictated by the 
microbes in your gut, so

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.791
we want to nurture them.

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:48.708
We actually harbor 
more microbes in our bodies

00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:49.791
than we have human cells.

00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:54.166
The question is, how do you 
foster diversity for better health?

00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:56.541
Well, to me, the 
answer is fermentation.

00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:58.000
Smells so good.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.125
Kimchi is just this superfood.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.041
Everyone should know 
how to make kombucha

00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:05.416
because of 
how simple it is.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.375
Put your hand on your belly 
now and take a deep breath in. 

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:12.875
That will change the 
habitat of the microbes.

00:01:12.916 --> 00:01:15.625
It's a mind-body technique.

